{
  "description": "A map of sets converted to an object type gets a list of numbers and a list of bools as defaults",
  "spec": [
    "ext/typeexpr/README.md#optional-object-attributes",
    "spec.md#collection-and-structural-type-conversions"
  ],
  "op": "eval",
  "features": [
    "typed-values",
    "functions",
    "type-expressions"
  ],
  "notes": "hashicorp/hcl unifies the map's elements and the added defaults before converting (unifyAsMap in ext/typeexpr/defaults.go). go-cty tries the two list types first, which fail because a list of numbers and a list of bools don't convert to each other, then settles on a set of strings (unify in cty/convert/unify.go), and the conversion to the object type turns the defaults back into lists.",
  "variables": {
    "m": {
      "map": {
        "a": {
          "set": [],
          "element_type": "string"
        },
        "b": {
          "set": [],
          "element_type": "string"
        }
      },
      "element_type": [
        "set",
        "string"
      ]
    }
  },
  "functions": {
    "convert": {
      "extension": "convert-with-defaults"
    }
  },
  "expect": {
    "valid": true,
    "body": {
      "attributes": {
        "a": {
          "object": {
            "a": {
              "set": [],
              "element_type": "string"
            },
            "b": {
              "set": [],
              "element_type": "string"
            },
            "c": {
              "list": [
                {
                  "number": "1"
                }
              ],
              "element_type": "number"
            },
            "d": {
              "list": [
                {
                  "bool": true
                }
              ],
              "element_type": "bool"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "blocks": []
    }
  }
}
